---
description: Never read or expose .env files or secrets in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

# Do not read env / secret files

- **Never** open, read, cat, or dump `.env`, `.env.*`, or files that clearly hold secrets (API keys, tokens, credentials).
- Prefer `.env.example` (placeholders only) when you need to know which variables exist.
- To debug env loading, check **key presence / string length only** — never print values.
- If a missing/empty env var breaks startup, tell the user to set it themselves; do not inspect the value.
- Never commit real secrets or paste them into chat, code, or docs.
